WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.968
-Henrik, welcome back to the
show and thanks for coming on.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.801
-Thank you.
-It's so -- It's so great

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.701
to have you in person,
because I knew this event's

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.467
coming up on Friday.
I didn't know if I'd

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.868
be able to see you before it,
but...

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.400
-Yeah.
-They're retiring your jersey.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.767
-It's amazing.
It's a surreal feeling,

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.834
you know, to have --

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:19.834
Obviously, the moment itself's
gonna be incredible.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.133
-Yeah.
-But also an opportunity

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:25.234
to bring all the people
to Madison Square Garden,

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:28.267
people that meant so much to me
throughout my journey --

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.968
friends, family,
and most importantly,

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:33.200
all the fans that supported me
throughout my career.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.734
It's gonna be amazing.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.033
How many people from Sweden are
coming to the Garden on Friday?

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.801
-Yeah, I think, as we speak,

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:40.934
they're pulling up to the hotel
right now.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.901
It's like 50, 60, people.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:46.300
We're gonna be around 100 people
at the game, 130, maybe, even.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.567
So...
-Really? Friends, family.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.434
-Friends, family,
a lot of friends in New York

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:54.467
and around the States,
they're flying in, so...

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.501
-Are you gonna have to
say something or no?

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.167
-Yeah, I'm gonna
say a few words.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.534
-Yeah.
-So we'll see how that goes.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.033
-Do you get --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:04.868
Do you get emotional?
-I do, at times.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.300
-Yeah.
-I think --

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.801
You know, when I played,
I was super-intense.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.634
-Yeah.
-I was an intense person.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.467
Preparation, playing the game.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.934
But I -- I felt a lot.
I played with a lot of emotions.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:19.167
And now, when I'm done playing,
you know,

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.968
I -- I still want
to feel those emotions.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:23.300
But it will be in different
settings, obviously.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.868
It won't be playing the game
and feeling that pressure.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:30.467
But I'm -- I'm still looking
for other ways to -- to feel.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:31.634
-But look at you.
You look great.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.467
I mean, you --
you left, I mean, on top.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.300
Was it --
Was it tough for you to go?

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.767
-You know, it was not my choice.
It was by health reasons.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.634
You know. About a year ago,
I had open-heart surgery.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:46.834
And it changed everything.
Obviously, I tried to come back.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.300
The surgery itself
went really well --

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.167
replaced a piece of my aorta
and a piece of my valve.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.234
-Wow.
-And I tried to come back.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.701
Unfortunately, I caught some
inflammation around my heart,

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.100
and that just made it too
difficult to come back and play.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.467
But I was in such a good place.
You know, I was so happy.

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:07.400
I was grateful for all
the things I experienced,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.834
especially here in New York
for so many years.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.834
So, you know, life's been great,
but it has definitely

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.434
been an interesting year for me,
no question.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.467
-Yeah, I --
I follow you on Instagram.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.834
And I saw this --
this post here.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:23.300
You said, "Yeah. Soon."
And I go, "Oh, wow."

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.567
And then, there's a picture
of you right here.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.334
-Yeah.
-This is probably where

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:29.534
they're gonna raise the jerseys,
right there.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.434
-Exactly.
So, first picture, you know,

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.400
looking at that arena,
Madison Square Garden,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.434
such a unique building, right?

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.601
There's so much --

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.534
so many different things
going on in there.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.434
Some days, we showed up
to the game,

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:43.667
and they were putting up
the boards

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.901
because the Knicks
played before us.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.267
I mean, the turnaround
in there is crazy.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.634
-Saw some of the best concerts
of my life there.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.734
-Oh, you see everything
in there.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:53.167
And it's such
an exciting place to play.

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.434
So I feel very blessed, you
know, to have that opportunity.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.634
-Now your number's
going up there.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.534
Your name is forever.
-Yeah, I know.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.734
-You're one of 11 Rangers
to be -- have their --

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:04.467
in the history of the Rangers
to have your jersey retired.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.133
-And that's the thing
with the Rangers.

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:09.868
Original six team.
They've always taken

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:13.033
a lot of pride in their history,
and you feel that as a player.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:17.367
You know, you come in as a young
kid from Sweden at 23 years old,

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:19.367
and I see all these
retired guys come by,

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:20.934
and they treat them so nicely.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.701
And it means something to them,
the history.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:26.000
And now,
to be part of that myself,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.734
it's kind of a surreal feeling.

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:29.801
But I remember the --
the second photo there,

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.400
I walked up to check it out
where my family's gonna sit

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.501
and where friends are gonna sit,
and right there

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.834
was all the banners, and that --

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.434
that was a very special moment
for me last week.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.767
-That's gonna be wild when
you're out on the ice there.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.901
I just -- I -- I know, also,

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:46.067
that you're doing
commentating now for MSG.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:50.801
And my question to you is --
is it tough for you to be

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:53.167
not one-sided when the Rangers
are playing someone...

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.834
...when you're doing
an interview?

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.334
Dude, I've heard you
caught a slip a couple times.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:58.467
-Yeah.
-And be like, "No, no.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:03:59.801
We're gonna come back,
and we're gonna --

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.968
I go, "You mean, the Rangers
can come back and win."

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, it's funny.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:06.167
You know, I think this
was the first or second time

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.234
I was there.
I asked the guys at the set,

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.734
"Do we say 'we,'
or do we say 'the Rangers'?"

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.567
Like, "No, no,
we say 'the Rangers.'

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:16.767
Even though we're Rangers
channel, we can't say "we."

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.667
Like, "Got it."
-Yeah.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.767
-Five times I said "we."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.133
-I was like, "I've been
doing it for 15 years."

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.534
-You're a Ranger.
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.868
-15 years,
I've said "we," you know?

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:30.434
-Well, we love you.
New York loves you.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.868
Hockey loves you.
Enjoy every second of it.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.467
It couldn't happen
to a better guy.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.601
And thanks for always
being a friend to the show.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:37.767
You're always welcome back.

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:40.434
-Thank you so much.
-Pleasure.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.133
Henrik Lundqvist, everybody!

